<article class="env-definition" id="00Z6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00Z6">Definition <span data-tag="00Z6">7.47.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $J$, $J'$ be two topologies on $\mathcal{C}$. We say that $J$ is <em>finer</em> or <em>stronger</em> than $J'$ if and only if for every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ we have $J'(U) \subset J(U)$. In this case we also say that $J'$ is <em>coarser</em> or <em>weaker</em> than $J$. </p>
